#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Recap: Simplifying Rational Exponents]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- Convert between rational exponent and radical form 🔄
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In this recap, we will review how to simplify rational exponents by converting them to radical form and vice versa.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Rational Exponent to Radical Form]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- $a^(m/n) = root(n, a^m)$
]
#only("2-")[
- Example: $16^(1/4) = root(4, 16) = 2$
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("To convert from rational exponent form to radical form, we use the formula a to the power of m over n equals the nth root of a to the power of m.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For example, 16 to the power of one-fourth equals the fourth root of 16, which simplifies to 2.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Radical Form to Rational Exponent]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- $root(n, a) = a^(1/n)$
]
#only("2-")[
- Example: $root(3, 27) = 27^(1/3) = 3$
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("To convert from radical form to rational exponent form, we use the formula the nth root of a equals a to the power of 1 over n.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For example, the cube root of 27 equals 27 to the power of one-third, which simplifies to 3.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Simplifying Expressions]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- Convert to the form that simplifies the expression
]
#only("2-")[
- Example: $(27^(1/3))^2 = (root(3, 27))^2 = 3^2 = 9$
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("When simplifying expressions with rational exponents, choose the form that makes the simplification easier.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For example, to simplify 27 to the power of one-third, all squared, we can first convert it to radical form, the cube root of 27, then square it to get 3 squared, which equals 9.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Summary]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[
- Rational exponent to radical form: $a^(m/n) = root(n, a^m)$ 📏
]
#only("2-")[
- Radical form to rational exponent: $root(n, a) = a^(1/n)$ 📐
]
#only("3-")[
- Simplify by choosing the more convenient form 🎯
]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("To recap, we can convert from rational exponent form to radical form using the formula a to the power of m over n equals the nth root of a to the power of m.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("We can convert from radical form to rational exponent form using the formula the nth root of a equals a to the power of 1 over n.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("When simplifying expressions, choose the form that makes the simplification easier. Practice these conversions to master simplifying rational exponents!")
]
]